+    // A well-formed dash pattern has a strictly positive period. A non-positive (or NaN, e.g.
+    // from an array mixing infinities) period means the pattern is degenerate - most commonly a
+    // non-empty, even-length array whose entries sum to zero or less (all-zero, or negative
+    // entries canceling out) - and has no well-defined dash/gap split. Treat it the same as an
+    // empty dash pattern: emit the input unchanged, rather than feeding `rem_euclid` a zero/
